instruction:
The side of the base \(ABCD\) of the regular pyramid \(SABCD\) is \(8\), and the height \(SO\) is \(3\). Point \(M\) is the midpoint of edge \(SB\), and point \(K\) is the midpoint of edge \(BC\). Find:
1) The volume of the pyramid \(AMSK\);
2) The angle between the lines \(AM\) and \(SK\);
3) The distance between the lines \(AM\) and \(SK\).
